What is CI/CD?
CI/CD = Continuous Integration & Continuous Deployment/Delivery
 It’s not a tool. It’s a practice.
When developers write code,
CI makes sure it gets tested & merged quickly.
CD ensures it gets deployed automatically without manual steps.
Goal: Ship features faster, safer, and more frequently.



What was it like before CI/CD?
Thoda socho...
 Developers worked on code for weeks or months
 Then came "merge day" – all code dumped together
 Nothing worked, bugs everywhere
 Manual testing
 Manual deployment
 Late night war rooms
 Blame game: “Dev ka problem hai.” → “No, Ops ka issue hai.”
 Tab release ek stressful event hota tha. Confidence zero.



What changed after CI/CD?
Everything.
CI caught bugs early.
CD automated deployment.
Teams started releasing daily, even hourly.
Less human error, more stability.
Devs & Ops started working together.
Industry got speed + safety — a powerful combo.



What is CI and what is CD?
CI (Continuous Integration)
Code changes from all developers are automatically tested & merged frequently.
CI ka kaam hai: “Code tootna nahi chahiye.”

CD (Continuous Deployment/Delivery)
Once code is tested, it's automatically deployed to staging or production.
CD ka kaam hai: “Code chale bina rukawat ke.”
